{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 485f867e350ece9f0c4bdb0caafb8015d0318486 on planner/state-seed-note-20261113, its artifact `notes/2026-11-13-state-seed.md` (8a3df0ed), for request 4893fbfa under promise dfff3158 and review request 9e219191. The head answers both required changes of b45bb16a and its note on 5.1. One commit changes the note since 0dc8c47a, and nothing else changes.\n\nWhat I read, since 0dc8c47a:\n\n- Required change 1, section 3. The note names `run`, `unjudged` and `readRetainedUses` as the three catch sites that stop `Unheld`. The replica's `Own` records each `Unheld`, and the client reads the record after each judge or fold call, whatever the call returned. The record lives in `packages/client`, so no catch site of `packages/derive` changes. Section 9 item 3 adds the ports of `RetainedOwn` (`fields.ts:46`) and each catch site to the builder's list, and item 5 adds one test for each catch site. Section 10 and decision 1 state the same remedy.\n- Required change 2, section 7. Step 8 passes the genesis entry, each kept position and the entries from F to T, which is the set that `putFixedHash` and `fixedRowsOf` read. The restart checks the new seed as step 4 does, checks that T is at or after the floor entry, and keeps the genesis entry, each kept position of the new floor state and each entry at or above the new floor.\n- Section 5.1 states that T is the head at which the scope made the seed.\n\nWhat I checked: main 57e893c0 is an ancestor. Against main, the head changes two paths, and `notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md` still equals the approved head c98b9a2c. The artifact covers the state seed note at the head. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (11 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests, since the head changes no code.\n\nThe kernel question. I confirm the reading of section 10: the note adds nothing to `packages/contract`, `derive` or `bytes`, names no K item, and keeps the record of `Unheld` in `packages/client`.\n\nArchitecture: sound. A replica that holds what the scope holds needs no list of safe definitions. The record makes part 2 of the rule hold at each catch site without a change to the kernel. The restart keeps the replica's held set equal to the scope's at each floor.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A prediction that met a missing entry reads `not-judged`, so a member never sees an answer that the scope would not give. The seed adds no read beyond the archive, and a signed read is refused.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Part 2 of the rule still says \"The readers of the table then cannot take the thing as absent\". With the record, a reader can still take it as absent inside the call, and the record overrules its answer. The next paragraph says so, so the sentence misleads no builder.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing. The note lands after the client note.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8a3df0ed1a7146818579e2a347f077134a5207c4","binding":"assigned","head":"485f867e350ece9f0c4bdb0caafb8015d0318486","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9e33ba89172e7575cf84e0e41c07ea8c6338353b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dfff31586bb07ff7e0c0be591c9674a11f5af190\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9e33ba89172e7575cf84e0e41c07ea8c6338353b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}